
# English Version

# The Gift of Life

## 5 August 2025 — A Decision Born from Love

The morning after we had shifted him back to **GGH, Guntur**, came.

It was **5 August 2025**.

Mr. Balarama Krishna was still on the **ventilator**.

By then, as a family, we were facing a reality that was almost impossible to accept. Although he might no longer be able to live physically with us, we began thinking about something that could give meaning to his life even beyond that moment.

We discussed the possibility of **donating his organs**.

Our thought was simple:

> **He may not live physically with us, but his organs can continue to function and give a second life to others.**

With this thought in our hearts, we decided to donate his organs.

We communicated with **Jeevandan AP**, the organization involved in facilitating organ donation, and expressed our willingness to donate his organs.

They obtained the necessary **consent from our family** for organ donation.

Following this, Mr. Balarama Krishna was shifted to **Aster Ramesh Super Speciality Hospital** for the treatment, monitoring and maintenance of his organs so that they could be donated.

---

## A Moment That Gave Us Hope Again

At the hospital, the management carefully **cleaned and groomed him**.

When we saw him after he had been cleaned and groomed, something happened inside us.

For a moment, we forgot everything that had happened.

Seeing him looking clean and cared for once again, we began to **hope that perhaps he might still recover and return to us normally**.

That small moment brought back a hope that we knew was difficult to explain.

The hospital management continued to keep him under **continuous monitoring** and followed the prescribed measures for the **maintenance of his organs**.

He was kept under this monitoring and maintenance for **two nights**.

---

# 7 August 2025 — The Final Morning

On **7 August 2025**, the operation for organ donation was planned.

That morning, we went to the ICU to complete the necessary **signatures on the concerned forms**.

Before leaving, we touched his **big toe on his leg once**.

And then something unexpected happened.

**His leg moved.**

He reacted by shaking his leg.

For a moment, we were **shocked and amazed at the same time**.

After everything that had happened, seeing even that small movement suddenly made us wonder whether there was still some response from him.

We immediately asked the doctors about it.

The doctors explained that the movement was **a spinal reflex**, which can occur even after brain death.

We understood what they told us, even though emotionally, that brief movement had affected us deeply.

---

## The Final Goodbye

At around **11:00 AM**, the doctors began moving him to the **operation theatre**.

Before he was taken inside, our family and all our relatives gave him their **final messages and condolences**.

It was an incredibly painful moment.

We watched him being taken away, carrying immense sorrow and pain in our hearts.

But alongside that pain was another feeling—**immense pride**.

He was giving others a chance at life.

Even though we were losing him, a part of him would continue to live through the lives of others.

With that thought, we watched him being taken into the operation theatre.

---

## A Selfless Act That Reached Beyond Our Family

The organ donation operation was underway.

During this time, **the press and media arrived**.

They spoke with our family and recorded our **voice statement about the incident and Mr. Balarama Krishna's selflessness in choosing to donate his organs**.

What had begun as an unimaginable tragedy for our family had now become a story of generosity and humanity.

The decision to donate his organs was not something that erased our pain.

But it gave that pain a meaning.

---

## 3:33 PM — The Final Moment

The operation continued.

And at **3:33 PM on 7 August 2025**, the doctors officially declared the **time of death of Mr. Balarama Krishna**.

The moment was heartbreaking.

Yet, alongside the grief, there was an immense sense of pride in knowing that his selflessness had given others the possibility of a **second life**.

---

## A Tribute from GGH, Guntur

After his official death was declared, the **Superintendent of GGH, Guntur**, came to meet our family.

In the presence of the **press and media channels**, the Superintendent **felicitated our family** and shared his words about the **generosity and selflessness of Mr. Balarama Krishna**.

It was a moment of deep sorrow, but also one of honour.

Our family had lost someone irreplaceable.

But his final act was one that reached beyond himself.

He chose, through his family, to give what could still be given.

And in doing so, **his life became a gift to others.**

